[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Recording an Earthquake]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.54]Lesson 42 | 第42课
[00:02.45]Recording an earthquake | 记录地震
[00:09.95]What does a pen have to do to record on paper the vibrations generated by an earthquake? | 要在纸上记录地震产生的振动，笔必须怎么做？
[00:18.95]An earthquake comes like a thief in the night, without warning. | 地震像夜间的窃贼一样，不打招呼就来了。
[00:23.69]It was necessary, therefore, to invent instruments that neither slumbered nor slept. | 因此，有必要发明既不打盹也不睡觉的仪器。
[00:29.84]Some devices were quite simple. | 有些装置相当简单。
[00:32.36]One, for instance, consisted of rods of various lengths and thicknesses which would stand up on end like ninepins. | 例如，有一种装置由长短粗细不同的棒组成，像九柱戏的木柱一样竖立着。
[00:41.06]When a shock came, it shook the rigid table upon which these stood. | 地震一来，这些棒所在的坚硬桌子就会晃动。
[00:46.36]If it were gentle, only the more unstable rods fell. | 如果震动轻微，只有较不稳的棒倒下。
[00:51.17]If it were severe, they all fell. | 如果震动剧烈，棒就全部倒下。
[00:53.99]Thus the rods, by falling, and by the direction in which they fell, | 这样，这些棒以其倒下和倒下的方向，
[00:58.85]recorded for the slumbering scientist the strength of a shock that was too weak to waken him, | 为沉睡中的科学家记录下了弱得不足以把他震醒的地震的强度，
[01:05.70]and the direction from which it came. | 以及地震来自的方向。
[01:08.99]But instruments far more delicate than that were needed if any really serious advance was to be made. | 但是，如果要取得真正重大的进展，需要比这精密得多的仪器。
[01:15.87]The ideal to be aimed at was to devise an instrument that could record with a pen on paper, | 要达到的理想是发明一种仪器，
[01:22.77]the movements of the ground or of the table as the quake passed by. | 能用笔在纸上记录当地震经过时地面或桌子的运动。
[01:28.24]While I write my pen moves, but the paper keeps still. | 我写字时笔在动，纸不动。
[01:32.57]With practice, no doubt, I could in time learn to write by holding the pen still while the paper moved. | 无疑，经过练习，我最终能学会纸动笔不动地写字。
[01:39.75]That sounds a silly suggestion, | 这听起来像个愚蠢的建议，
[01:42.31]but that was precisely the idea adopted in some of the early instruments (seismometers) for recording earthquake waves. | 但这恰恰是早期一些记录地震波的仪器（地震仪）所采用的想法。
[01:51.70]But when table, penholder and paper are all moving, how is it possible to write legibly? | 可是，当桌子、笔杆和纸都在动时，怎么可能写得清楚呢？
[01:59.02]The key to a solution of that problem lay in an everyday observation. | 解决这个问题的关键在于一个日常的观察。
[02:04.18]Why does a person standing in a bus or train tend to fall when a sudden start is made? | 为什么站在公共汽车或火车上的人在车子突然启动时会跌倒？
[02:10.59]It is because his feet move on, but his head stays still. | 那是因为他的脚跟着前移，而头还留在原处。
[02:15.18]A simple experiment will help us a little further. | 一个简单的实验可以帮助我们进一步理解。
[02:18.39]Tie a heavy weight at the end of a long piece of string. | 在一根长绳的一端系上一个重物。
[02:22.24]With the hand held high in the air, hold the string so that the weight nearly touches the ground. | 把手高高举在空中，握住绳子，让重物几乎碰到地面。
[02:28.78]Now move the hand to and fro and around but not up and down. | 现在让手前后左右晃动，但不要上下动。
[02:33.76]It will be found that the weight moves but slightly or not at all. | 会发现重物几乎不动或根本不动。
[02:38.34]Imagine a pen attached to the weight in such a way that its point rests upon a piece of paper on the floor. | 设想把一支笔以某种方式固定在重物上，笔尖触在地板的一张纸上。
[02:44.93]Imagine an earthquake shock shaking the floor, the paper, you and your hand. | 设想地震的震动摇晃着地板、纸张、你和你的手。
[02:51.42]In the midst of all this movement, the weight and the pen would be still. | 在所有这一切运动当中，重物和笔将是静止的。
[02:55.97]But as the paper moved from side to side under the pen point, its movement would be recorded in ink upon its surface. | 但当纸在笔尖下来回移动时，纸的运动就会以墨水记录在纸面上。
[03:04.18]It was upon this principle that the first instruments were made, but the paper was wrapped round a drum which rotated slowly. | 第一批仪器正是根据这个原理制造的，不过纸是包在一个缓慢旋转的鼓上的。
[03:13.20]As long as all was still, the pen drew a straight line, | 只要一切静止，笔就画出一条直线，
[03:17.64]but while the drum was being shaken, the line that the pen was drawing wriggled from side to side. | 但当鼓被震动时，笔所画的线就会左右扭动。
[03:25.18]The apparatus thus described, however, | 然而，如此描述的装置
[03:27.85]records only the horizontal component of the wave movement, which is, in fact, much more complicated. | 只记录了波浪运动的水平分量，而实际的波浪运动要复杂得多。
[03:35.21]If we could actually see the path described by a particle, | 如果我们真能看到一个质点描绘的轨迹，
[03:39.21]such as a sand grain in the rock, | 比如岩石中的一粒沙，
[03:41.95]it would be more like that of a bluebottle buzzing round the room; it would be up and down, to and fro and from side to side. | 那它更像一只绿头苍蝇在房间里嗡嗡乱飞的路线；它会上上下下、前前后后、左左右右。
[03:50.54]Instruments have been devised and can be so placed that all three elements can be recorded in different graphs. | 人们已经设计出一些仪器，并且可以这样放置：所有三个分量都能记录在不同的图纸上。
[03:58.84]When the instrument is situated at more than 700 miles from the earthquake centre, | 当仪器安置在离震中700多英里的地方时，
[04:04.62]the graphic record shows three waves arriving one after the other at short intervals. | 图形记录显示三个波相继到达，间隔很短。
[04:10.63]The first records the arrival of longitudinal vibrations. | 第一个波记录的是纵向振动的到达。
[04:15.56]The second marks the arrival of transverse vibrations which travel more slowly and arrive several minutes after the first. | 第二个波标志着横向振动的到来，这种振动传播较慢，在第一个波之后几分钟才到达。
[04:25.16]These two have travelled through the earth. | 这两种波都是在地球内部传播的。
[04:27.87]It was from the study of these that so much was learnt about the interior of the earth. | 正是从对这两种波的研究中，人们对地球内部才有了那么多的了解。
[04:33.66]The third, or main wave is the slowest and has travelled round the earth through the surface rocks. | 第三种波即主波最慢，是沿地表岩石环绕地球传播的。
